    {
      "chunkIndex": 2,
      "contentPreview": "HOW TO RE-MEASURE -- do NOT do this by arithmetic on the byte count. The cap compares against CHARS, not bytes:      $raw = [System.IO.File]::ReadAllText(\u0027src/Scrinia.Mcp/Prompts/guide.md\u0027)     $raw.Length                      # chars -- the number the cap compares against     ($raw.ToCharArray() | ? { [int]$_ -gt 127 }).Count   # non-ASCII  Each em-dash is 1 char but 3 bytes, so it contributes 2 EXTRA bytes. 48 em-dashes = 96 extra bytes: 8142 - 96 = 8046. Getting this wrong is exactly how the",
